## AI-Assisted

## Isolates users' temporary and shm directories. Every login for a user will
## see the same variant of the directory, but different users will see
## different variants.
##
## https://www.kicksecure.com/wiki/Dev/Strong_Linux_User_Account_Isolation
## man namespace.conf

## Root reached by elevation (sudo, su -) gets the SYSTEM instance of these
## directories, not the calling user's. The pam-config (namespace-security-misc)
## runs a second, uid-0-gated `pam_namespace.so unmnt_only` that unshares and
## unmounts the inherited per-user binds, so root never silently operates inside
## a mount view an unprivileged user primed (a categorical privilege-escalation
## surface). The caller's own session is unaffected (the unmount happens in the
## elevated process's fresh namespace).
##
## Accepted consequence: a user->root /tmp handoff such as
## `echo x >/tmp/f; sudo cat /tmp/f` no longer works. Do both sides as root,
## redirect in the caller (`sudo cat </tmp/f`), or use a non-/tmp path.

/tmp       /run/pam-namespace/tmp-inst/   user:iscript=/usr/libexec/security-misc/pam-namespace-init   root
/var/tmp   /var/tmp/tmp-inst/             user   root
/dev/shm   /run/pam-namespace/shm-inst/   user   root
